course: dictionary
lesson: 14212
title: Multiplied in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can work out what a word means by reading the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «Sam multiplied 3 by 4 and got 12.» The numbers and the answer 12 are the clues, so multiplied must mean a number was taken a certain number of times.
explain: «The rabbits multiplied all summer.» There are no numbers here, but the word summer and the result tell you that multiplied means grew greatly in number. Ask yourself: what word would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Multiplied is the past form of multiply. Multiply, multiplies, multiplied and multiplying all come from the same word, so they mean the same kind of thing, just at different times. Look for words like «by» or «together» near it, as in «multiplied by» or «multiplied together».
fact: Multiplied means a number was taken a certain number of times.
fact: «3 multiplied by 4 is 12.»
fact: The answer when you multiply numbers is called the product.
fact: Multiplied also means grew greatly in number, as in «the rabbits multiplied».
fact: In science, «cells multiply» means cells make more copies of themselves by splitting in two.
exercise: «Sam multiplied 3 by 4 and got 12.» What does multiplied mean here? | Added 4 to 3 | *Took 3 four times over | Took 4 away from 3 | Shared 12 by 3
exercise: «The rabbits multiplied all summer.» What does multiplied mean? | *Grew greatly in number | Fell asleep | Got smaller | Ran away
exercise: 5 multiplied by 2 is what? | 7 | 3 | *10 | 52
test: «Cells multiply by splitting in two.» What does multiply mean in this science sentence? | Stop growing | Turn into water | *Make more copies of themselves | Shrink to nothing
test: 4 multiplied by 4 is what? | 8 | 0 | 44 | *16
exam: The product is the answer when numbers are multiplied: what is 6 multiplied by 3? | *18 | 36 | 63 | 9
